# PROJECT: CAMPUSCONNECT — COLLEGE EVENTS & OPPORTUNITIES DISCOVERY PLATFORM

Act as a senior full-stack software engineer, UI/UX designer, database architect, and application security engineer.

Build a modern, responsive, production-oriented web application for a college Event Coordinating Team. The platform helps students discover events and opportunities published by colleges, universities, companies, and other organizations.

The application must contain TWO SEPARATE WEB PORTALS:

1. STUDENT PORTAL — Public-facing website for discovering events and opportunities.
2. EVENT TEAM PORTAL — Private administration website for the authorized college Event Coordinating Team.

Both portals must share the same database, event data model, visual identity, and application infrastructure.

The primary event-editing interface must be Google Sheets. Authorized event coordinators maintain the master spreadsheet. A Google Apps Script integration synchronizes valid spreadsheet records into the database. Students must never need an account to browse events.

Do not build only a static UI mockup. Build a functional application with reusable components, realistic sample data, proper routing, responsive layouts, loading states, error states, and a clear integration structure for the backend.

