DATABASE SECURITY:

Implement Row Level Security policies.

Public users must only be able to read events that are published and otherwise eligible for public display.

Public users must not be able to:
- Insert events.
- Update events.
- Delete events.
- Read private synchronization errors.
- Read admin profiles.
- Read private integration configuration.

Only authorized server-side processes and authorized administrators may perform protected operations.

Never trust a client-side role flag as the sole authorization mechanism.

Protect all admin endpoints with real server-side authentication and role checks.

Use the minimum necessary database permissions.

